\title{gPIPE: PIPE designs for drug-combination dose finding}
\description{
gPIPE implements the PIPE design (product of independent beta
probabilities escalation) for dose-finding trials of drug combinations,
for any number of drugs.
}
\details{
\itemize{
\item \code{\link[=DoseGrid]{DoseGrid()}} sets up the dose combinations and their partial order.
\item \code{\link[=ms_design]{ms_design()}} sets up the original PIPE design of Mander and Sweeting
(2015) for the maximum tolerated dose (MTD) contour, and
\code{\link[=cheung_design]{cheung_design()}} the PIPE design with epsilon-tapering of Cheung et al.
(2022) for the minimum effective dose (MED). \code{\link[=PipeDesign]{PipeDesign()}} gives full
control over the settings.
\item \code{\link[=estimate]{estimate()}} and \code{\link[=next_dose]{next_dose()}} work on the data of a running trial, and
\link[=simulate.PipeDesign]{simulate()} gives operating characteristics.
}

See \code{vignette("gPIPE")} for a worked example.
}
